{
 "about": "Beta overlay merge vectors (docs/r2-plan.md section 9; shared contract rule 2). state = the job's raw entry in stages-beta.json (the beta's own file), overlay = the job's raw entry in v1's stages.json (read-only); null = no entry. Merged entry = the state entry, except its stage comes from the overlay when the overlay has a valid stage AND (the state entry has no sat OR overlay.at > sat, strictly). Items (assess, lane, cut, asphalt, pavers, cleanup, removed) come only from the state entry. stage = the merged entry's effective stage; stageFrom = where it came from (overlay | state | none); effective = effective(merged, hints null), same as contract_vectors.json; keepWhenClosed = keepWhenClosed(effective). Times: an ISO 8601 date-time with Z or a +-HH:MM offset, compared as instants to the millisecond (JS Date.parse); a sat that is missing, null, not a string or not such a time counts as NO sat; an overlay at that is missing or unreadable is never newer. 'times' lists parse results in epoch ms (null = not a time). sync_jobs.py (merge_entry, parse_time) and js/stages.js must both produce exactly these results. Only the RAW string counts: no trimming (a leading space or a trailing newline makes it no time). Impossible calendar times (2026-02-30, 2026-09-31, hour 24, minute / second / offset minute 60, year 0000) are no time either (JS Date.parse accepts some of them; js/stages.js cleanIso rejects them like Python). Neither app writes such values (both use toISOString); they only come from hand edits.",
 "version": 1,
